                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Similar presentation to Bullet Sorrow, you teleport to next fixed point after taking out enemies that rush in. There's a sequence where you're moving on  a crane gantry but most of the time you're standing in the middle of the room. Enemies move to use cover so it's a little frustrating not to have any cover yourself. You're wearing a helmet (there's a HUD in the field of view) so presumably the suit can take a lot of damage and it's possible to dodge incoming fire when the game switches to bullet time.\n    weapons are fixed - an assault rifle and shotgun, reload by pressing the trackpad. Enemies look good and distant enemies are outlined in red so they're easier to see, there's a good sense of size in some of the larger areas. \n   If you like the Bullet Sorrow style of play you'll probably like this. More weaponry with a traditional reload style would have been good imo as would more creative use of cover and the ability to move but that's not what this style of game is about. It's a satisfying blast for $5.",
